# Styling

Brutalist and print-inspired: 1px ink borders, zero border-radius, offset drop shadows instead of
blur, one acid-lime accent, paper-grid background, chromatic aberration on display type.

## Tokens only

- **No hardcoded colors outside `src/routes/layout.css`.** Use `var(--ink)`, `var(--paper)`,
  `var(--accent)`, `var(--on-accent)`, `var(--muted)`, `var(--inverse)`, `var(--on-inverse)`.
- Tints come from `color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 32%, transparent)`, not a new hex value.
- Layout widths use `--site-shell-max`, `--site-shell-pad-x`, `--site-content-max`,
  `--site-content-max-wide`, `--site-sidebar-width` so the header and pages stay aligned.
- New token → add it to both `:root` and `.dark` in `layout.css`.
- The one exception is canvas rendering, which cannot read custom properties; `Waveform.svelte`
  takes accent from the `accentColor` store and `--ink` / `--paper` via `getComputedStyle`, and
  re-applies fills when the theme or accent changes.

## Scoped CSS, not utilities

- Style inside the component's `<style>` block with semantic class names (`.auth-intro`,
  `.form-error`).
- Tailwind is installed but effectively unused in components. Do not convert scoped CSS to utilities,
  and prefer scoped CSS for new work.
- Expose variation as a custom property rather than a boolean prop:
  `<SiteHeader --site-header-gap="0" />`.

## Dark mode

- Class-based on `<html>` via `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))`.
- **Verify every change in both themes.** Accent-on-paper is the known contrast trap — that is what
  `.eyebrow-chip` exists for.
- Do not touch the pre-paint script in `src/app.html` unless you intend to; it prevents a flash of
  the wrong theme.
- Theme flips animate via the `.theme-transition` class added to `<html>` for 320ms, because custom
  properties cannot transition.

## Reuse the utilities

`.display-face` (Audiowide), `.eyebrow`, `.eyebrow-chip`, `.accent-fill` / `.accent-text` /
`.accent-border`, `.pressable`, `.glitch-mark` (needs a matching `data-text` attribute).

An `h1.display-face` gets chromatic fringes automatically — do not re-implement it.

## Non-negotiables

- Buttons and inputs stay square: `border-radius: 0`, `1px solid var(--ink)`. Raised paper panels use
  `border: 1px solid var(--hard-border)` and `box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 var(--hard-shadow)` (ink in light,
  accent edge + darkened accent shadow in dark). Cover art uses `--cover-shadow` instead (ink in
  light, translucent ink in dark — not accent-tinted). Accent-filled pressables keep an ink border so
  the edge stays visible on the fill; their shadow still uses `--hard-shadow`.
- Never remove focus styling. `:focus-visible` is a `2px solid var(--ink)` outline with `3px` offset.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. CSS animation is already covered by a global rule; JS-driven
  motion must check `window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)')`.

Details: `docs/design-system.md`.
